PIPO Register

Implemented a 4-bit Parallel-In Parallel-Out (PIPO) register in Verilog.

The register:
* Loads all 4 input bits simultaneously on the rising edge of the clock.
* Holds the stored value until the next rising edge.
* Uses sequential RTL with a non-blocking assignment (<=).
* Represents four D flip-flops operating in parallel.

A testbench was created to apply different 4-bit inputs, and the behavior was verified using Icarus Verilog and GTKWave.

Files
* pipo.v - PIPO register RTL
* pipo_tb.v - Testbench for simulation